WEBVTT

01:39.900 --> 01:41.510
Where am I?

01:47.380 --> 01:50.750
Huh? Damn it!

01:54.500 --> 01:55.850
Who's there?

02:01.520 --> 02:02.140
What?

02:14.550 --> 02:15.900
Anarchy-chan?

02:16.200 --> 02:17.400
Anarchy-chan!

02:17.910 --> 02:18.900
Are you oka—?

02:19.910 --> 02:21.290
Anarchy-chan...

02:22.760 --> 02:24.400
You must have had a scary dream.

02:24.400 --> 02:26.040
I don't know!

02:26.040 --> 02:29.200
It's okay. It's okay now.

02:39.500 --> 02:43.040
That magical girl, Slayer or whatever,
that's what she said.

02:43.310 --> 02:45.170
I'll give you a single day.

02:46.430 --> 02:51.060
We don't have much time left. Just one day?

02:51.060 --> 02:53.100
One day means,

02:53.100 --> 02:56.600
since the battle yesterday 
was around 11 at night,

02:55.690 --> 02:58.690
Train Schedules

02:56.600 --> 02:58.690
twenty-four hours after that?

02:58.690 --> 03:01.640
Nobody cares about your dumb 
train schedules, asshole.

03:01.640 --> 03:05.200
It's not like we're battling 
the Yamanote line.

03:05.200 --> 03:08.540
Either way, it means this is the end.

03:08.540 --> 03:11.930
I guess we're really gonna die.

03:11.930 --> 03:14.960
You saw what happened yesterday. That thing.

03:15.690 --> 03:20.520
From the start, they could have 
killed us whenever they wanted.

03:20.520 --> 03:24.460
They've playing with us like toys!

03:33.090 --> 03:34.600
What are you talking about?

03:35.480 --> 03:40.730
This crap about how we're going to 
die, how this is the end...

03:40.730 --> 03:44.270
Oh, ouch!

03:45.600 --> 03:48.220
That's hot! It burns! Ouch!

03:48.220 --> 03:51.200
Ow! What! What!

03:55.700 --> 03:57.280
What the hell you doing?

03:57.280 --> 03:59.430
Take it easy, Otaku Hero.

04:06.800 --> 04:09.990
I know you're trying to cheer us up.

04:09.990 --> 04:10.920
But still...

04:10.920 --> 04:12.930
This is already an unbeatable game.

04:12.930 --> 04:14.440
It isn't unbeatable at all!

04:17.600 --> 04:21.760
We moved so many people's hearts 
with our Wanku! event.

04:21.760 --> 04:25.700
That wasn't a lie. That's our power!

04:25.930 --> 04:29.520
So you're saying we still 
have some way to win?

04:29.520 --> 04:31.460
We do! We definitely do.

04:32.290 --> 04:36.010
Tomorrow, before the enemy attacks here, 
we attack their headquarters.

04:36.010 --> 04:36.950
And then...

04:37.500 --> 04:39.120
we take out Shobon!

04:39.320 --> 04:40.650
Take out Shobon?

04:41.480 --> 04:42.390
When this started,

04:42.390 --> 04:46.430
the moment that guy appeared, 
the whole world lost its mind.

04:46.880 --> 04:48.890
It was like everyone was brainwashed.

04:49.480 --> 04:51.130
I've been wondering about that.

04:51.130 --> 04:55.040
Why were we the only ones 
who didn't change at all?

04:56.190 --> 04:57.260
Could it be because...

04:57.260 --> 04:59.150
Now that you mention it, you might be right!

04:59.150 --> 05:01.890
If the enemy's goal is 
to eliminate all otaku,

05:01.890 --> 05:05.030
all they would have to do 
is brainwash us, too.

05:05.460 --> 05:08.990
I bet they realized 
that we can't be brainwashed.

05:08.990 --> 05:12.520
That's why they have no choice 
but to attack us directly.

05:12.520 --> 05:16.040
So there's still hope, then.

05:16.040 --> 05:18.950
If there's a way to win, that's gotta be it.

05:18.950 --> 05:22.540
If Slayer is coming here, 
their base will be undermanned.

05:22.730 --> 05:24.800
So right when they're attacking here—

05:24.800 --> 05:26.320
no, even before that,

05:26.320 --> 05:28.050
if we hit their headquarters directly

05:28.050 --> 05:29.910
and get rid of Shobon,

05:29.910 --> 05:32.600
there's a good chance it'll 
undo all the brainwashing!

05:32.960 --> 05:35.410
That's frickin' awesome, Otaku Hero!

05:35.410 --> 05:38.060
I'm starting to feel like 
we might have a chance!

05:38.060 --> 05:41.230
You're making me feel like you 
are our real leader!

05:41.230 --> 05:43.950
I actually am your real leader, you know.

05:43.950 --> 05:46.280
But what a blind spot!

05:46.280 --> 05:49.200
And here we thought the enemy 
always had the upper hand.

05:49.560 --> 05:53.700
I never realized we had special 
anti-brainwashing powers!

05:53.890 --> 05:56.840
It's like we got a new cheat skill!

06:00.780 --> 06:04.090
But why didn't it affect 
us in the first place?

06:04.090 --> 06:07.510
Because we always had our own things 
that we really, truly like.

06:07.510 --> 06:09.590
Things we really, truly like?

06:09.910 --> 06:14.940
It takes a lot of strength 
to really know the things you enjoy!

06:14.940 --> 06:16.640
You might have a point.

06:16.640 --> 06:18.600
I get the feeling that you're right!

06:18.930 --> 06:21.320
Our actions now will change the world.

06:21.890 --> 06:24.150
We're going to take things back 
with our own otaku hands,

06:24.150 --> 06:26.160
and return to a world with no Shobon!

06:27.160 --> 06:30.910
A world where we can like what 
we want as much as we want!

06:30.910 --> 06:33.790
Yeah!

06:33.790 --> 06:34.720
Say what...

06:34.720 --> 06:35.520
...ever!

06:35.520 --> 06:36.240
We want to...

06:36.240 --> 06:36.960
like!

06:36.960 --> 06:37.790
As much as...

06:37.790 --> 06:38.790
we like!

06:38.790 --> 06:39.520
Say what...

06:39.520 --> 06:40.230
ever!

06:40.230 --> 06:40.930
We want to...

06:40.930 --> 06:41.600
like!

06:41.600 --> 06:42.550
As much as...

06:45.360 --> 06:47.550
Cheers!

07:21.190 --> 07:22.790
You know, to be honest,

07:23.160 --> 07:27.420
I haven't even gone to that new 
Railway Museum that just opened yet.

07:27.770 --> 07:30.260
It kinda feels like it's both 
too close and too far.

07:30.260 --> 07:33.470
I think if I go, it'll 
lose some of its magic.

07:33.470 --> 07:35.430
Nah, you should just go.

07:35.430 --> 07:37.400
It's just a bunch of trains lined up.

07:37.400 --> 07:38.800
Even I've been there.

07:38.800 --> 07:41.920
Well, that area is under enemy control.

07:42.220 --> 07:44.520
For now, that does make it far away.

07:47.110 --> 07:48.810
Fine, I made up my mind!

07:48.810 --> 07:53.440
When this battle is over, 
I'm going to the Railway Museum!

07:55.620 --> 07:57.410
Flag! That's a huge flag!

07:57.410 --> 07:58.560
Death confirmed!

07:58.560 --> 08:01.020
Aww! Darn it!

08:01.020 --> 08:03.460
Yeah, but I don't know.

08:03.830 --> 08:07.450
We're probably all gonna die this time.

08:07.450 --> 08:11.700
In a situation like this, 
a flag might not be a flag at all.

08:11.700 --> 08:13.520
If I was the director...

08:12.340 --> 08:14.030
You ain't the director, man!

08:15.220 --> 08:17.800
Well if I can say another flag-raising line,

08:17.800 --> 08:20.090
there might still be an ending 
where we survive.

08:23.220 --> 08:25.360
Okay. Fine, then.

08:25.610 --> 08:28.730
When this battle is over, 
I'm gonna buy an arcade PCB!

08:28.730 --> 08:31.240
I'm gonna produce an underground idol!

08:31.240 --> 08:34.240
I'm gonna re-open 
the Akiba Transportation Museum!

08:34.240 --> 08:36.320
I'm going to open my own maid cafe!

08:36.320 --> 08:38.480
I'll turn Akiba into a town 
for electronics parts again!

08:38.480 --> 08:40.480
I'll open a plastic-model-themed cafe!

08:41.600 --> 08:43.620
I-I'm gonna...

08:43.620 --> 08:46.070
When this battle is over,

08:49.160 --> 08:51.760
I'm taking Yuririn on a date!

08:53.440 --> 08:55.510
That isn't your call, man.

08:55.510 --> 08:57.440
And Yuririn's right here, too.

09:03.000 --> 09:04.100
No chance!

09:05.880 --> 09:06.820
He's dead!

09:06.820 --> 09:08.350
He died before he died!

09:13.400 --> 09:16.210
I won't be able to see 
you girls for a while.

09:17.560 --> 09:19.000
But what's bothering me is,

09:19.450 --> 09:22.070
why did they just leave instead
of finishing us off?

09:22.790 --> 09:25.650
I'm worried they might 
have something planned.

09:26.060 --> 09:28.880
Anyway, Slayer is coming for real this time.

09:28.880 --> 09:30.140
Please be carefu—

09:29.160 --> 09:30.140
You know what?

09:30.360 --> 09:33.600
You keep talking about 
how much you're worried for us,

09:33.600 --> 09:36.930
but to be completely honest, 
we're more worried about you.

09:37.380 --> 09:39.640
Yeah, you're taking 
the words out of our mouths.

09:39.640 --> 09:42.230
Gobo gobo, gobo gobo...

09:40.380 --> 09:43.050
"Even with all the troops, 
you're still the leader."

09:44.300 --> 09:45.640
You might be right.

09:45.640 --> 09:46.800
But anyway,

09:46.800 --> 09:48.400
we'll be okay.

09:48.400 --> 09:52.040
Just focus on your objective, Otaku Hero.

09:54.950 --> 09:56.080
I hear you.

09:56.480 --> 09:58.150
A li'l motorboating to get you started?

09:58.150 --> 09:59.330
Eh, I'm fine, actually.

10:00.810 --> 10:02.710
Bogo bogo?

10:05.210 --> 10:07.110
I think I'm good there, too.

10:07.820 --> 10:10.350
We're planning to leave before dawn.

10:11.410 --> 10:13.960
Okay, girls, I'll see you later.

10:15.290 --> 10:17.220
You know, I honestly

10:17.220 --> 10:20.720
think I was born to fight this battle.

10:20.720 --> 10:22.600
So that's why, Otaku Hero,

10:22.600 --> 10:25.110
since you want to protect this place,

10:25.110 --> 10:26.840
we'll protect it for you.

10:28.220 --> 10:29.850
Yeah. I'm counting on you.

10:52.810 --> 10:55.030
Let's go over the plan one more time.

10:55.500 --> 10:59.320
The magical girl team will stay in Akiba 
to defend against Slayer.

11:00.560 --> 11:02.880
Akiba will be mostly abandoned.

11:02.880 --> 11:05.560
Don't worry about collateral damage,
just fight with everything you got!

11:05.960 --> 11:08.550
That's what we were already planning to do!

11:09.280 --> 11:13.070
I'll take the Revolutionary Army 
to SSC's main base

11:13.340 --> 11:15.180
and attack the National Diet Building!

11:15.180 --> 11:16.320
Yes, sir!

11:24.150 --> 11:27.290
Nick will be monitoring us 
and Anarchy's team

11:27.290 --> 11:28.800
to provide back-up.

11:28.800 --> 11:30.440
You're in good hands!

11:43.800 --> 11:45.970
Our target is the head of SSC,

11:45.970 --> 11:47.560
Shobon himself!

11:48.720 --> 11:51.190
If anyone gets in our way, take them out!

12:02.720 --> 12:04.750
<i>Got the weather satellite data.</i>

12:04.750 --> 12:06.860
<i>Clouds above the Nagatacho 
area will be clearing</i>

12:06.860 --> 12:08.370
<i>in 180 seconds!</i>

12:11.880 --> 12:13.340
<i>Thirty seconds!</i>

12:15.330 --> 12:16.720
<i>Fifteen seconds!</i>

12:21.160 --> 12:22.350
<i>Nine...</i>

12:22.350 --> 12:23.360
<i>Eight...</i>

12:23.360 --> 12:24.410
<i>Seven...</i>

12:24.410 --> 12:24.970
<i>Six...</i>

12:25.380 --> 12:25.960
<i>Five...</i>

12:26.360 --> 12:27.390
<i>Four...</i>

12:27.390 --> 12:28.390
<i>Three...</i>

12:28.390 --> 12:29.210
<i>Two...</i>

12:29.430 --> 12:30.350
<i>One...</i>

12:30.350 --> 12:30.840
<i>Zero!</i>

12:30.840 --> 12:33.940
Revolutionary Otaku Army, attack!

12:33.940 --> 12:40.950
Yeah!

12:41.520 --> 12:42.700
Here they come!

12:42.700 --> 12:44.240
Hold them off!

13:04.470 --> 13:05.980
Well, look who's here.

13:05.980 --> 13:09.710
Hey, aren't you a little 
earlier than scheduled?

13:09.710 --> 13:13.360
Weren't you the ones planning an ambush?

13:14.760 --> 13:18.150
Oh, I see you brought some friends along.

13:18.150 --> 13:20.260
Gobo gobo?

13:18.640 --> 13:20.260
"Too scared to come alone?"

13:21.680 --> 13:25.990
Shobon-sama ordered me to bring these two.

13:28.040 --> 13:32.160
But I could squash you 
all by myself if I wanted!

14:15.950 --> 14:17.290
Gobo gobobo!

14:21.880 --> 14:24.290
Go... gobo? Gobo!

14:28.180 --> 14:32.570
Hold on. Akiba's gonna be flattened!

14:32.570 --> 14:33.920
<i>We're at the Diet building!</i>

14:44.190 --> 14:45.480
We've broken through.

14:45.480 --> 14:47.830
Now heading inside the Diet build—

14:54.500 --> 14:55.320
Don't stop!

14:57.870 --> 15:00.010
Get wrecked!

15:00.980 --> 15:02.440
Go ahead, Otaku Hero!

15:02.440 --> 15:03.680
We've got this area cov—

15:15.000 --> 15:16.020
We've made it!

15:16.020 --> 15:17.080
What are you doing?

15:17.080 --> 15:17.520
Hurry and open it up!

15:17.520 --> 15:18.610
<i>Hurry and open it up!</i>

15:19.040 --> 15:22.890
This security... These guys aren't amateurs.

15:22.890 --> 15:25.410
But I ain't new here, either.

15:27.070 --> 15:27.900
<i>Door is open!</i>

15:39.920 --> 15:42.200
Hey! Is this the right way?

15:42.200 --> 15:43.240
<i>No question!</i>

15:43.240 --> 15:44.920
<i>That's the fastest way to the core!</i>

15:44.920 --> 15:46.160
That must mean...

15:49.300 --> 15:50.800
Wah! Ah!

15:50.800 --> 15:55.120
Ow, ow, ow, ow! Ouch! Uh.

15:57.800 --> 15:59.220
What the heck?

15:59.620 --> 16:03.680
Even with three of ya, you can't keep up.

16:14.510 --> 16:17.120
Gobo bobo bobo bobo, gobo bobo bobo bobo...

16:16.620 --> 16:18.030
<b>GAME</b>

16:17.120 --> 16:18.370
Gobo bobo!

16:18.980 --> 16:19.620
Go?

16:26.560 --> 16:28.750
Go... go!

16:29.320 --> 16:30.310
<i>Gobo?</i>

16:44.680 --> 16:47.680
Huh? What... was that?

16:51.810 --> 16:55.120
Gobo, bo!

17:02.440 --> 17:04.370
Go-Gobo?

17:10.520 --> 17:12.210
Blue? Pink?

17:12.210 --> 17:15.550
Yeah, where'd they go? At a time like this!

17:15.550 --> 17:18.810
You think you have time 
to be looking around?

17:19.040 --> 17:23.130
Keep your eyes on me, you little shit!

17:26.570 --> 17:27.680
What the hell?

17:28.260 --> 17:33.320
I do all of this for Shobon-sama, 
trying to please him,

17:34.440 --> 17:37.080
but the more I do...

17:37.950 --> 17:44.060
Why does this piss me off so much?!

17:52.740 --> 17:54.460
Is that what this is?

17:54.460 --> 17:55.260
Huh?

17:55.260 --> 18:00.370
When I'm fighting with you, 
it almost feels like I'm fighting myself.

18:01.360 --> 18:04.630
Maybe that's why it always 
makes me feel this way.

18:09.040 --> 18:11.340
We're in bullet hell right now!

18:11.340 --> 18:13.810
<i>That's the only way into the core!</i>

18:13.810 --> 18:15.510
<i>Do what you have to to get through!</i>

18:15.510 --> 18:16.980
Easy for you to say!

18:16.980 --> 18:19.000
Fire!

18:22.890 --> 18:23.740
What was that?

18:23.740 --> 18:24.750
What just happened?

18:26.240 --> 18:27.750
It's you guys!

18:28.460 --> 18:30.580
What a filthy room.

18:30.970 --> 18:33.580
Just like my pad when I was a kid.

18:33.580 --> 18:36.090
Whoa, wh-what do you think you're—?

18:36.090 --> 18:38.710
<i>Can you hear me, brothers?</i>

18:38.710 --> 18:40.720
<i>Mansei Bridge Otaku Commune!</i>

18:40.720 --> 18:42.720
<i>We've joined the Revolutionary Army!</i>

18:43.990 --> 18:47.430
<i>Assist Otaku Hero!</i>

19:03.170 --> 19:05.030
<i>Yeah, like that, Otaku Hero!</i>

19:05.030 --> 19:07.520
<i>Shobon's location is straight ahead!</i>

19:07.520 --> 19:11.300
Of course you won't let us go easily, I say!

19:11.300 --> 19:13.280
Quit dragging your feet, Otaku Hero!

19:13.280 --> 19:14.540
Victory is just ahead!

19:20.180 --> 19:21.090
Opening it now.

19:21.090 --> 19:21.800
Do it!

19:23.550 --> 19:25.580
Go for it!

19:25.580 --> 19:29.180
Otaku Hero!

19:33.490 --> 19:36.350
Man, this is a dramatic climax!

19:36.350 --> 19:38.440
The tide is turning in our fav—

19:49.830 --> 19:52.460
How could... All of a sudden?

19:52.460 --> 19:54.480
Gobo...

20:01.210 --> 20:02.860
I'm calling the win.

20:32.610 --> 20:34.620
Wh-What is this?

20:34.620 --> 20:36.780
<i>What happened? Was Shobon there?</i>

20:36.780 --> 20:38.500
<i>Hey, Otaku Hero!</i>

20:43.130 --> 20:46.140
otaku hiding

20:43.130 --> 20:46.140
Explosion

20:43.130 --> 20:46.140
Smoke clears
and

20:43.130 --> 20:46.140
silhouettes of
Four Heavenly
Kings on top
of building

20:46.140 --> 20:47.640
Opens box and

20:46.140 --> 20:47.640
Anarchy looks exhausted

20:46.140 --> 20:47.640
Otaku Hero surprised

20:46.140 --> 20:47.640
Stands in front of
Otaku Hero

20:46.140 --> 20:47.640
Otaku Hero panics and
covers his eyes

20:46.140 --> 20:47.640
Magical girls unbothered

20:46.680 --> 20:47.770
A diary?

20:48.010 --> 20:49.140
Otaku salute
Otaku Hero
and the
others' victory

20:48.010 --> 20:49.140
We've
retaken
Akihabara!

20:48.010 --> 20:49.140
Anarchy and
Otaku Hero

20:48.010 --> 20:49.140
Wow!

20:48.010 --> 20:49.140
Flag fluttering
on top of building

20:48.010 --> 20:49.140
The otaku win

20:48.010 --> 20:49.140
Otaku Hero thumbs up

20:48.010 --> 20:49.140
Anarchy winks

20:49.130 --> 20:50.440
No.

20:50.440 --> 20:53.860
A record of what's happened so far?

20:54.170 --> 20:56.700
Huh? What does this mean?

20:54.890 --> 20:57.400
Chogo-shi typing
notes on tape

20:54.890 --> 20:57.400
Cardboard box
by showcase has

20:54.890 --> 20:57.400
figurines thrown away with
empty cup noodle containers

21:05.780 --> 21:07.780
If something happens, use these.

21:07.780 --> 21:09.790
Gobo gobobo!

21:08.110 --> 21:09.790
Yeah, we'll take them.

21:10.130 --> 21:13.000
But it should be an easy win without them!

21:15.620 --> 21:17.210
All otaku around yelling, continues

21:15.620 --> 21:17.210
All hands, attack!

21:15.620 --> 21:17.210
otaku attack

21:25.850 --> 21:29.280
We <i>are</i> gonna die after all!

21:29.280 --> 21:31.680
Did you already forget what you said before?

21:31.680 --> 21:32.310
Huh?

21:32.310 --> 21:36.680
Aren't you taking me on a date 
when the battle's over?

21:36.680 --> 21:38.680
Yu-Yuririn!

21:44.320 --> 21:45.740
Yuririn!

21:50.160 --> 21:51.330
Anime Otaku
screams

21:50.240 --> 21:52.240
He gets up slowly,
in a daze, but

21:52.370 --> 21:53.700
Gets shot

21:53.100 --> 21:54.480
In a moment,

21:54.480 --> 21:57.460
the limited express train 
"Fellow Traveler" will be departing,

21:57.980 --> 21:59.780
bound for hell.

21:59.780 --> 22:03.220
Please board the train in a timely—

22:12.220 --> 22:14.970
Anarchy

22:12.220 --> 22:14.970
Drinks

22:13.050 --> 22:14.960
What the hell is this?

22:15.260 --> 22:19.240
He could have, at least, 
made it a tastier-looking color.

22:19.590 --> 22:21.190
Otaku Hero,

22:21.190 --> 22:23.690
since you want to protect this place,

22:23.690 --> 22:25.160
we'll protect it for you.

22:25.360 --> 22:29.490
If that's how I can see you smile again...

22:31.300 --> 22:32.610
You can't!

22:32.610 --> 22:36.440
<i>Answer me! Otaku Hero! What happened?</i>

22:36.440 --> 22:40.100
<i>Hey, Otaku Hero! Otaku Hero!</i>

22:40.100 --> 22:43.710
You can't... take those!

22:41.460 --> 22:43.710
Rampaging magical girls
 They start to change shape

22:44.150 --> 22:49.960
You can't!

23:25.210 --> 23:27.430
Wow, this is so fun. Just dandy!

23:27.430 --> 23:29.280
But I'm seriously getting 
tired of this shit.

23:29.280 --> 23:31.540
Ugh, I'm so bored.

23:31.540 --> 23:35.560
The middle part was okay, but I can't 
take much more of this crap.

23:35.560 --> 23:39.940
Oh. Wait. What? Huge plot twist.
